hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1722","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Aban, narrated to us Wakee’, who said: Ishaq ibn ‘Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to me, who said: Isma’il ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn ‘Atiyah al-Ansari narrated to me, who said: My grandmother narrated to me, that:

When the Prophet (ﷺ) gathered the women of the Ansar in a house, ‘Umar (RA) came to us and stood at the door and greeted us. We returned his greeting, so he said, “I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to you all.” So we said, “Welcome to the Messenger of Allah and his messenger.” He said, “Will you pledge to me that you will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery?” They said, “Yes.” So we extended our hands from inside the house, and he extended his hand from outside.

**CHAPTER:**"
"1723","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qaysi: narrated to us Abu 'Asim, from Ishaq ibn 'Uthman, in a similar manner (though he did not say: ""Do not associate anything with Allah"").

She ('A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her) said:
""We were commanded to bring out the menstruating women and the young, unmarried women on the two 'Eids, and we were forbidden from following funeral processions, and there is no Friday prayer upon us (women).""

I said to her: ""What is the *ma'ruf* (recognized good) from which you were forbidden?""
She said: ""Wailing (niyahah).""

**CHAPTER:**"
